# 12. RACI Governance Rules

The following rules apply:

1. Each major activity must have at least one **Accountable** role.
2. Responsibility may be assigned to multiple participants where execution requires collaboration.
3. Business-process decisions remain accountable to the appropriate business owner.
4. Technical implementation is accountable to the Developer / Technical Lead.
5. Product priorities remain accountable to the Product Owner.
6. End users are consulted during usability and UAT activities.
7. RACI assignments should be reviewed when project scope or stakeholder responsibilities change.

